# File: tests/blender/test_pivot_reseat.py
# Generated from: specs/244-let-finalize-fix-or-tolerate-a-millimetre-scale-pivot-bottom-center-offset-on-rigged-meshes/requirements.md
Feature: Rigged assets with a millimetre-scale pivot offset finalize cleanly

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A millimetre-scale offset on a rigged mesh no longer blocks finalize
    Given rigged asset "Hero" at rest with its bottom center at (0.0006, 0.0013, -0.0007)
    When authored validate runs and then the Desktop cleanup of the variants step
    Then validate reports no pivot.bottom_center finding
    And the Desktop bottom center is within 1 mm of the world origin

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: The re-seat moves only mesh data
    Given the offset rigged asset with a second skinned part parented to SM_Hero
    When the Desktop cleanup re-seats the mesh
    Then every part's mesh data moves by the same world offset
    And object transforms, modifiers, vertex groups and weights, and bones are unchanged

  @SCN003
  Scenario: A rigged asset already on the origin is left alone
    Given rigged asset "Hero" exactly on the origin
    When the Desktop cleanup runs
    Then its vertex positions are unchanged
    And the report says no re-seat was needed

  @SCN004
  Scenario: A large offset still fails clearly
    Given rigged asset "Hero" with its bottom center 2 cm above the origin
    When authored validate runs
    Then pivot.bottom_center fails and names the 5 mm re-seat limit

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Static assets keep their current behavior
    Given static asset "Crate" offset 1.3 mm and then 0.8 mm from the origin
    When authored validate and the Desktop cleanup run
    Then the 1.3 mm crate fails pivot.bottom_center and the 0.8 mm crate passes
    And the static Desktop mesh is not re-seated

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Exported variants agree
    Given the offset rigged asset after the variants step
    When export-time validate, export, and the re-import check run
    Then no pivot.bottom_center or reimport pivot finding is reported for Desktop or Mobile
